  "worked_solution": "The left-hand side is a perfect square. Therefore, we can solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-6)^{2} & =-9 \\\\ x-6 & =\\pm \\sqrt{-9} \\\\ x-6 & =\\pm 3\\,\\text{i} \\\\ x & =6\\pm 3\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has two solutions, $x=6+3\\,\\text{i}$ and $x=6-3\\,\\text{i}.$",
